#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0227 expect=noViolation domain=CM
#note "Pins the NEW inner-join semantics: subject 005 has CMENRF populated and NO DM record at all. Under the removed Join_Type: left, DM.RFENDTC was null after the merge and this rule fired with a factually wrong message; the inner join drops the row instead -- D-TA-2 (inner is the doctrine): a subject absent from DM is the referential-integrity rule's finding, not this rule's -- one root cause, one finding. The unmatched subject is reported by CDISC-CG0029. DM is present and non-empty (subject 001, RFENDTC populated), so a rule that still left-joined WOULD fire here: this is a discriminator, not a vacuous pass."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset CM class=INTERVENTIONS label="Concomitant/Prior Medications"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col CMSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col CMTRT   type=Char label="Reported Name of Drug, Med, or Therapy"
col CMENRF  type=Char label="End Relative to Reference Period"
---
S1 | CM | 005 | 1 | ASPIRIN | AFTER
---

dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFENDTC type=Char label="Subject Reference End Date/Time"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2020-06-30
